cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Wound Segmentation Deep Learning Model with Clinical Validation"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-01-20"
url: "https://github.com/yourusername/wound-segmentation-model"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yourusername/wound-segmentation-model"
license: MIT
abstract: |
  A specialized YOLOv8-based deep learning system for automated wound segmentation
  in clinical images. This capstone project focuses on clinical validation,
  statistical rigor, and TinyML deployment optimization. The system fine-tunes
  YOLOv8n-seg architecture using a compiled dataset of 2,760 wound images from
  three validated sources, implementing custom Focal Tversky Loss and comprehensive
  statistical analysis including Wilcoxon signed-rank tests, Bootstrap confidence
  intervals, and Bonferroni corrections for multiple comparisons.

